-- title:
--   Commutativity from a stable line only after base change
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ and $F'$ be fields, let $e \colon F \to F'$ be a ring homomorphism, let $\iota$ be an index type, and let $M \colon \iota \to \mathrm{M}_2(F)$ be a family of $2 \times 2$ matrices over $F$ indexed by $\iota$. Assume: (i) the family has no common stable line over $F$, in the sense that for every nonzero $v \in F^2$ there is an index $i$ with $M_i v$ outside the $F$-submodule generated by $v$ (here $M_i v$ is the matrix–vector product `Matrix.mulVec`); (ii) there is a vector $u \in F'^2$ with $u \neq 0$ such that, for every index $i$, the entrywise image $e(M_i)$ of $M_i$ satisfies $e(M_i) u \in F' \cdot u$, i.e. $u$ spans a line over $F'$ stabilised by every $e(M_i)$. The conclusion is that the whole family commutes: $M_i M_j = M_j M_i$ for all $i, j \in \iota$. Note that $e$ is an arbitrary ring homomorphism of fields, hence injective, and no finiteness or nonemptiness is assumed of $\iota$.
--
--   This is the elementary linear-algebra fact that a family of $2 \times 2$ matrices which becomes reducible (acquires a common stable line) after base change, but is irreducible over the ground field, must be commutative. It is used in [`GaloisRep.forall_stableLine_false_of_irreducible_of_det_inertia_pow_odd`](thm.html#GaloisRep.forall_stableLine_false_of_irreducible_of_det_inertia_pow_odd) to rule out a common stable line for a Galois representation over a larger coefficient field.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Matrix_mul_comm_of_forall_map_mulVec_mem_span_of_forall_exists_mulVec_not_mem_span.lean

